Mechanical Testing and Evaluation — ASM Handbook, volume 8 (@metal-asm-testing: 0, is #reference, #part-of @metal-sources) { r_1VW327STC5YQGRAPNRAPQSZQNG
Howard Kuhn and Dana Medlin, editors. Mechanical Testing and Evaluation, ASM Handbook volume 8, ASM International, 2000. DOI 10.31399/asm.hb.v08.9781627081764. [Publisher's handbook and full contents](https://dl.asminternational.org/handbooks/edited-volume/47/Mechanical-Testing-and-Evaluation) · [Publisher contents PDF](https://www.asminternational.org/wp-content/uploads/files/06772G/06772G-toc.pdf).

An optional commercial source for complete professional test methods, equipment, specimen/fixture effects, uncertainty, data interpretation, tension/compression, hardness, impact, fatigue/fracture, creep, and specific component/joint tests. Study complete applicable chapters and compare with the open NIST guides and graduate course. Use the actual applicable test-standard edition for a practical study; a dated handbook does not establish every current requirement.

Editors, volume, date, DOI, contents, and access classification verified on 29 October 2026. No free full-text access or blanket reuse licence is claimed. All source material remains external.

